From 2f6b0674fd15bf21373eaea0b7e9bad129855149 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tendai Makumire <121951760+tmakumire@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 May 2025 10:38:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Added support for AR1335 on CSI4 and CSI6 (#51)

The CSI4 and CSI6 camera slots on the SBC
are connected to I2C buses from an I2C switch.
Before we can communicate with the sensor, the I2C channel
on the switch must first be selected. So every I2C Write
or Continuous I2C write must first set the I2C switch channel.
The simplest way would be to just add this to the sensor XML
but we would need somewhere to specify the channel for the particular
for the channel. Ideally this would go in the module XML rather
than the sensor XML. But as temporary workaround, we have put
it into the XML. The major problem with this workaround is that
we need a separate sensor XML for each I2C channel. And it
also doesn't work with more than 1 sensor. This is because
the exposure driver doesn't take a slave address parameter
so it doesn't allow us to set the channel. So we can only
have 1 sensor working when using the slots with the I2C switch.

The sensors not sitting on slots behind an I2C switch work
as normal and we can have multiple sensors.
